# Build output of the `guinea` makefile target. `make clean` deletes it, and
# the README tells every contributor to build it, so it is not a repo file.
# guinea_nofftw, histogram.o and memory.o are deliberately committed and stay
# tracked despite also being clean targets.
/guinea

# Python bytecode caches. A stale one for docker/make_hepmc.py used to be
# committed, which is worse than useless once the source changes.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
